<h1><span lang="EN-GB">ModelMaker D/C Hardware Assembly</span></h1>
<div class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;" align="center">
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3"></div>
<h2>Handling the ModelMaker sensor</h2>
<p id="P4" class="Warning"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font id="font1">ModelMaker is a precision optical measuring instrument, please treat it with care.</font></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-GB">The ModelMaker sensor has been designed to withstand a typical shop-floor environment, nevertheless, there are certain precautions that should be taken when using the sensor:</span></span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;">Do not drop the sensor.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-GB">Do not touch the optical windows on the front of the sensor.</span></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;">Do not attempt to dismantle the sensor. Doing so will invalidate the &#160;warranty.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-GB">Do not allow the sensor to be covered in any liquid</span></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-GB">Do not expose the sensor to extremes of temperatures</span></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Warning" id="P1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-GB">Laser light is emitted from the indicated aperture - do not look directly into the beam or view with an optical instrument.</span></span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-GB">ModelMaker hardware set-up</span></span></h2>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps"><span lang="EN-GB">If not already completed, the first step is to set up the <a href="arm_types_mmd.htm">localiser</a></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps"><span lang="EN-GB">Power up the localiser before starting the ModelMaker hardware set-up.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps"><span lang="EN-GB">Power up the sensor. There are two LEDs on the rear of the sensor: Power (red) and Laser (yellow) - see the image below. The Power LED will start flashing fast - this means that MM D/C is still booting and not ready to be connected to the PC.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="font-family:Arial;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;">When the Power LED begins flashing slow this means that the sensor is ready to accept connection.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps"><span lang="EN-GB">Connect the sensor cable to the Ethernet port of the PC. Then Power LED will be on when connection is established.</span></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="Example"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">MM D/C Power LED</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP166565458" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="MMD_LEDs.gif" width="272px" height="279px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-GB">Voice control microphone</span></span></h2>
<p class="Note" id="p5"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: This feature is unsuitable for use in a noisy environment.</span></span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">A sound card is required to use this feature and Microsoft Speech SDK v5.1 must be installed (provided on the KUBE CD or can be downloaded from www.microsoft.com).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;">A microphone is supplied with the ModelMaker D/C system.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Warning" id="P3"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;">Ensure the battery is installed and the microphone switched on.</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt; font-family:Arial;">Before using this feature please setup the microphone using Control Panel &gt; Speech on your PC. Select</span> Speech Recognition &gt; Configure microphone and follow the configuration 'wizard'. Experiment with the position of the microphone so it is close to your mouth but not directly in front of it.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="mso-ansi-font-size:12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;"><img src="speech1.gif" width="78px" height="51px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""> &#160;To use voice operation in KUBE click on the speech icon in</span> System &gt; Preferences &gt; Audio.</p>
<p><img src="speech2.gif" width="80px" height="52px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""> &#160;In the localiser scan menu, click on the microphone button to enable it.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">The keywords and commands available are all those words found in the Scan menu e.g. 'Prescan', 'Scan', 'View' etc. During Scan mode: 'Start' to start scanning and 'Stop' to pause.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">The speech recognition software is developed by Microsoft. Please refer to the Microsoft help files for more information.</p>
</li>
</ul>
